8-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":13,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":14,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"## Apply the standard","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":15,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":16,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Put every class in a package. Use lowercase package names rooted at the project name, `luke`, followed by logical","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":17,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  subgroup names when the code is split into components.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":18,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Name classes and enums with PascalCase nouns, methods with camelCase verbs, variables with camelCase English names,","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":19,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  booleans to read as booleans, collections with plural nouns, and constants with SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":20,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Use four spaces, never tabs. Keep lines below the 120-character hard limit and aim for fewer than 110 characters.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":21,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  Indent wrapped lines eight spaces beyond their parent line and wrap at readable, high-level boundaries.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":22,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Use K\u0026R braces. Always brace loop and conditional bodies, and put conditional bodies on separate lines.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":23,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- For this project, align `case` and `default` labels with their enclosing `switch`, and indent their statements one","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-27T00:12:51","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":24,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  level further. End each case with `break` or use an explicit `// Fallthrough` comment when fallthrough is intentional.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-27T00:12:51","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":25,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Put spaces around operators and after Java keywords, commas, and `for`-loop semicolons. Separate logical units with","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":26,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  one blank line.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":27,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Attach array brackets to the type. Initialize variables at declaration when practical and declare them in the","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":28,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  smallest useful scope. Do not expose non-constant class variables publicly unless the class is a behavior-free data","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":29,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  class.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":30,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- List imports explicitly, remove unused imports, and keep import ordering consistent. Group static imports first,","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":31,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"  followed by ordinary imports grouped consistently by package family.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-26T23:56:33","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":32,"author":{"gitId":"lukelouyu"},"content":"- Write English 